  DEFENDING ARMY

  Standing tall with his warriors was Teleko.  Lady of Beer Mbaba stood 
determinedly at the head of her thousands.
  Teleko stepped forward and challenged Mbaba to personal combat.  
Lady of Beer Mbaba answered the challenge to honorable combat.  Teleko 
chanted his mysterious words of magic and cast a Spiritwrack spell, to make 
Mbaba quake and shiver with spiritual convulsions.
  Mbaba loped along steadily and closed to bow range.  Chanting his words of 
magic with trained precision, Teleko let fly a Holy Symbol spell.  A golden 
mist in the shape of a cross formed around Teleko.
  Mbaba closed to melee range, filled with uncontrolled blood-lust.  Mbaba 
swang at Teleko but Teleko evaded the sword.  Teleko attempted to help his 
cause with a Hand Of Death spell, but it sputtered at the last second.  
Mbaba thrust at her nemesis but her aim was just off the mark.  Teleko 
turned away Mbaba with his spirited assault.  He then swang at Mbaba with 
maximum force and missed by a mile.
  Mbaba treacherously thrust at Teleko but her sword whiffed through the 
air.  Teleko daringly swang at Mbaba and inflicted 5 damage points.  Mbaba 
maneuvered for a better attacking vantage.  Then Mbaba swang at Teleko with 
all her might and scored 1 damage points on Teleko.  Teleko flamboyantly 
vaulted over Mbaba and contemptuously swang at her and would have struck her 
if Mbaba hadn't sidestepped.
  Showing no fear, Mbaba swang at Teleko but Teleko evaded the blow.  Teleko 
swang at Mbaba but his aim was just off.  Mbaba faked one way, then switched 
over and swang at Teleko and scored on him, doing 1 points of damage.  
Teleko violently assailed Mbaba and damaged her, scoring 4 damage points.
  With amazing speed, Mbaba thrust at Teleko and walloped him with 1 damage 
points.  Teleko summoned all his strength and bravely swang at his nemesis 
and inflicted 5 damage points.  Mbaba was fatally wounded.  And so it was 
that Mbaba met her tragic end.
  The forces commanded by Lady of Beer Mbaba were disheartened by her 
demise, but still they moved forward with some hope of victory.  As luck 
would have it, Teleko's formations were well hidden by a sudden mist, giving 
them a small edge.  Also, tactical supremacy was guaranteed by Teleko's 
powerful tactical genius.
  The Dragons commanded by Teleko were not impressed by his strange 
appearance.  The Orcs commanded by Mbaba were disgusted with her strange 
appearance.
  Out on the right flank, the Veteran 323rd Trolls were arrayed against the 
Veteran 67th Legion.  The 323rd Trolls battled with the 67th Legion and 
drove them back with a savage fury.
  Within the interior front, the Veteran 320th Eagles were arrayed against 
the 15th Phalanx.  The 320th Eagles soared over the 15th Phalanx and 
attacked them.  The 320th Eagles battled the 15th Phalanx and smashed their 
heads as if they were eggplants.
  Within the interior lines, the 322nd Eagles faced the Crack 234th Legion.  
The 322nd Eagles swooped down on the 234th Legion and attacked without 
mercy.  On this field, an officer of the 322nd Eagles noticed an opening in 
the enemy lines which had opened when they skirted a wide rock formation.  
Charging into the gap, the 322nd Eagles gained a considerable advantage.  
The 322nd Eagles battled the 234th Legion and gradually pushed them back.
  In the interior front, the Veteran 319th Eagles were arrayed against the 
235th Legion.  The 319th Eagles soared over the 235th Legion and attacked 
them.  The 326th Dragons swooped down on the 235th Legion and attacked them. 
The 319th Eagles battled with the 235th Legion and cut them down like 
beanstalks.
  On the left outside flank, the 321st Eagles faced the 261st Phalanx.  The 
321st Eagles swooped down on the 261st Phalanx and attacked them.  The 321st 
Eagles fought the 261st Phalanx and squashed them like rotten oranges.
  Having found a vulnerable spot in the line of the host of Mbaba, a final 
savage slashing attack defeated their enemy and won the day for Teleko.  The 
323rd Trolls annihilated the 67th Legion.  The 320th Eagles destroyed the 
15th Phalanx.  The 322nd Eagles scattered the 234th Legion in all 
directions.  The 319th Eagles slew the 235th Legion almost to a man.  The 
321st Eagles demolished the 261st Phalanx.
  Teleko's well-planned campaign accomplished the conquest of Limerick.  Its 
forces completely destroyed, the acting commander escaped alone to the 
Daedalus Sea.

  An army coming from the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) 
entered the Daedalus Sea, hoping to conquer that province owned by 
Lady of Beer Mbaba and made up of great Plains.  Teleko (#72)'s forces 
encountered little resistance in the Daedalus Sea and Teleko there 
established our rule.  Teleko leads approximately 1 Dragons, 4 Eagles and 2 
Trolls.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) invaded the province of Berga, a 
Desert area ruled by Lady of Beer Mbaba.  Teleko (#72)'s forces encountered 
little resistance in Berga and Teleko there established our rule.  Teleko 
leads approximately 1 Dragons, 5 Eagles and 1 Trolls.
  Thus endeth the adventures of Lady of Beer Mbaba for this year.


  Mbaba treated with her ally Bradipo I (#2).  Mbaba treated with her ally 
Hokuto (#4).  Mbaba treated with her ally Prometeo (#5).  Mbaba treated with 
her ally Kahn (#6).  Mbaba treated with her ally Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  
Mbaba treated with her ally Circe (#8).  Mbaba treated with her ally 
Agesilao (#9).
  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  The 213th Chariots helped a local count of Chirfa to subdue a native tribe 
and rose to Average quality.


  Here is the financial report for Mbaba's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 12 gold in revenue.  3 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  3
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Mbaba was left with 43 gold in 
the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Berthier, Squire to Samantha
To: Mbaba

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter gave way to spring.  Samantha moved into Kabompo (#804) with her 
redoubtable Fleet.

  A fleet coming from the empire of Lady of Beer Mbaba entered Kabompo, 
hoping to subjugate that province ruled by 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) and made up of great Seas.  Samantha
's naval forces took control of Kabompo practically uncontested.  Kabompo 
was discovered to have a tax base of 3 gold.
  In early summer, Samantha moved into the Amazonian Sea (#905) with her 
Fleet.  East of here lies the province of the Virgo Sea (#1005), ruled by 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  It is known to be a Forest province 
occupied by Elves.  Their Elven fighters array themselves as Axemen and 
Heavy Cavalry.  To the southeast lies a Forest province called the Mermaid 
Sea (#906), populated by Elves.  It is ruled by 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  Their Elven warriors prefer to fight as 
Bowmen and Heavy Cavalry.  Turning to the southwest, one espies a Forest 
area, which is known as the Buccaneer Sea (#806).  It is populated by Elves 
and Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll rules there.  Their Elven warriors 
array themselves in the style of Bowmen and Fleet.

  Ships bearing the battle-standards of the Mbabaian empire cruised into the 
Sea province of the Amazonian Sea, a land defended by the forces of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  Samantha's naval forces took control of 
the Amazonian Sea practically uncontested.  The Amazonian Sea was found to 
have an income of 4 gold.
  With the coming of the late summer season, Samantha invented nothing in 
her sagely experiments.
  During fall, Samantha invented nothing valuable in her sagely experiments.
  The fall darkened into early winter.  Samantha invented nothing in her 
sagely researches.

  Thy humble servant,   Berthier, Squire to Samantha


